# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Both of these hold something that must not travel with the
# history, and neither is reliably confined to bin/.

# The debugging profile passes JID, password and endpoint on the command line
# - a working account in plain text, one 'git add' away from the history. It
# is a local file by nature: whoever checks the project out brings their own
# account, not this one.
**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# The OMEMO store: the secret IdentityKey, every PreKey and every chain key,
# and unencrypted at that. Whoever reads the file reads the conversations
# along with it. It is written next to the executable, which today means bin/
# - but only for as long as nobody publishes anywhere else.
omemo-*.json

# The chat logs from --chatlogs, and the files fetched with --storeChatMedia.
# The directory is chosen on the command line and usually lies outside this
# tree, so this catches only the obvious case: somebody who passes a relative
# name and lands inside the checkout. It is the conversations themselves - and
# with --storeChatMedia every photo anybody sent - so once is enough.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is not tidiness. Written as
# 'chatlogs/' this pattern matches at every depth, and git on Windows compares
# without regard to case - so it swallowed XMPPConsole/ChatLogs/, the source
# directory of the feature, and the whole of it would have quietly stayed out
# of the commit.
/chatlogs/
/chat-logs/
